WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:16.095
From the watch list
on the monitor tab,

2
00:00:16.095 --> 00:00:17.850
click the underlying
symbol you wish

3
00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:20.355
to create your options trade for.

4
00:00:20.355 --> 00:00:23.540
So long as your tabs are part
of the same Windows group,

5
00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:26.895
the underlying will appear
in the order entry panel.

6
00:00:26.895 --> 00:00:29.145
To the right of the
order entry panel,

7
00:00:29.145 --> 00:00:31.930
select option chain from
the drop-down menu.

8
00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:33.480
The option chain display,

9
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.380
shows call options to the left,

10
00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:36.905
and put options to the right

11
00:00:36.905 --> 00:00:38.995
of the central strike column.

12
00:00:38.995 --> 00:00:41.720
You will see the price
and the daily change of

13
00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:44.665
the underlying to the
upper right of the window.

14
00:00:44.665 --> 00:00:46.295
Above the call area,

15
00:00:46.295 --> 00:00:48.995
you will see tabs for
different explorations.

16
00:00:48.995 --> 00:00:52.820
Click a tab or to locate
additional exploration dates,

17
00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:55.135
click on the, "More" tab.

18
00:00:55.135 --> 00:00:57.060
Above the port area,

19
00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:00.045
you will see a drop down
menu for strike prices.

20
00:01:00.045 --> 00:01:02.810
Access this menu to change or

21
00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:06.410
refine the number of strike
prices displayed on the page.

22
00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:08.270
Hovering the cursor above

23
00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:11.135
any bid price displays
a red background.

24
00:01:11.135 --> 00:01:14.105
This indicates that by
clicking on the field,

25
00:01:14.105 --> 00:01:17.405
it would create an order
to sell that option.

26
00:01:17.405 --> 00:01:19.760
Hovering above any ask price,

27
00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:21.290
displays a blue background

28
00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:23.600
indicating that by
clicking on this field,

29
00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:26.635
it would create an
audit to buy an option.

30
00:01:26.635 --> 00:01:30.725
Locate the design option
strike you want to transact,

31
00:01:30.725 --> 00:01:32.825
click on the relevant
price field,

32
00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:35.765
which will close the
option chain display.

33
00:01:35.765 --> 00:01:37.670
Use the order entry panel to

34
00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:40.295
define the quantity
of options to trade.

35
00:01:40.295 --> 00:01:43.925
Choose the right order type
from the drop down menu.

36
00:01:43.925 --> 00:01:45.965
If you're using a limit price,

37
00:01:45.965 --> 00:01:47.600
choose the value by clicking in

38
00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:50.770
the input field or simply
typing in the value.

39
00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:53.580
Select from the time
and force drop down

40
00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:56.520
whether this is a
day or a GTC order.

41
00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:58.710
Your order is ready to review.

42
00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:00.350
Click the, "Submit" button to

43
00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:02.555
generate an order confirmation.

44
00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:06.280
When you have reviewed the
details, click, "Transmit."

45
00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:08.270
The order is sent for execution

46
00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:09.740
at the exchange and will appear

47
00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:13.250
in the activity panel to
the lower left of mosaic.

48
00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:16.085
To pause or interact
with an act of order.

49
00:02:16.085 --> 00:02:17.900
Click on it in the activity panel

50
00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:20.460
and make the relevant choice.